# Journal, zenray-cop-designer (append only, never rewritten)

Each entry: date in English, what was asked, what was decided, what was measured. Corrections are new entries that cite the old one.

## 11 October 2026 : first request, build overnight, Substance and Copernicus

- 11 October 2026, request (Matthieu, paraphrased): build a Python tool that reproduces the reference height as well as possible and that produces REAL Copernicus nodes (not a PNG export), focused on the height graph only; document every Copernicus feature from the web; code until morning; resume through a cron every 15 seconds if the code stops; use workflows or Haiku subagents; the tool must use only the functions of the platform.
- 11 October 2026, decision: the tool writes its own graph format (IR) and compiles it into real `copnet` nodes with hython. A Python file cannot be turned into a graph automatically; the designer writes the graph directly, so the nodes are the real ones.
- 11 October 2026, decision: the node inventory is read from the installed Houdini 22.0.368 (384 Copernicus nodes, 10 064 parameters), not from memory or from a web list. Web pages are used for summaries only.
- 11 October 2026, measured: the designer's window graph equals the SimpleHeight L05 export with maximum difference 0.0. Baseline EQUIV 0.373.
- 11 October 2026, measured and rejected: an EQUIV-driven search reached 0.61 by adding fine streaks; the planche looked worse. Decision: the search objective became statistical, inside look limits. Lesson: a score that the search can see is a score it will game.
- 11 October 2026, not possible: strict identity with the reference, under the no-copy rule and with random placement of chips.
- 11 October 2026, watchdog: cron tools cannot run below 60 seconds, so a background watchdog checks every 15 seconds and relaunches the optimizer.
- 11 October 2026, open: Substance Designer is not installed; its mapping is documented, not executed. Look limits wait for Matthieu's validation.

## 11 October 2026 : v2 search pushed against its look limits, gradient weight lowered

- 11 October 2026, measured: v2 (run window_opt_2) reached score 0.162 and EQUIV 0.471 with grain gain, grain length and chip size all on their look limits. The planche showed speckled dust and fine scratches. Cause: the gradient term (weight 0.25) rewards high-frequency energy. Decision: weight 0.05, run window_opt_3. v2 kept as evidence.

